# Event Management System Diagrams

This document contains architectural and conceptual diagrams for the Event Management System. The diagrams are generated using Mermaid syntax.

## 1. Entity-Relationship (ER) Diagram
This diagram outlines the database tables, their columns, and how they relate to one another.

```mermaid
erDiagram
    USERS ||--o{ EVENTS : organizes
    USERS ||--o{ BOOKINGS : makes
    USERS ||--o{ EVENT_REGISTRATIONS : joins
    USERS ||--o{ EVENT_REVIEWS : writes
    USERS ||--o{ NOTIFICATIONS : receives
    USERS ||--o{ USER_TOKENS : owns
    
    CATEGORIES ||--o{ EVENTS : categorizes
    
    EVENTS ||--o{ BOOKINGS : has
    EVENTS ||--o{ EVENT_REGISTRATIONS : has
    EVENTS ||--o{ EVENT_REVIEWS : receives

    USERS {
        int id PK
        string name
        string email
        string phone
        string password
        string role "Admin/Organizer/Customer"
        string status
    }

    EVENTS {
        int id PK
        int organizer_id FK
