        int id PK
        int user_id FK
        string token
    }
```

## 2. UML Class Diagram
This captures the core classes in your application logic. Note that `User` acts as the superclass for different distinct roles.

```mermaid
classDiagram
    class User {
        +int id
        +String name
        +String email
        +String phone
        +String password
        +String role
        +String status
        +login()
        +register()
        +updateProfile()
    }
    
    class Admin {
        +manageUsers()
        +manageEvents()
        +manageCategories()
        +viewReports()
    }
    
    class Organizer {
        +createEvent()
        +updateEvent()
        +viewAnalytics()
        +manageMyEvents()
    }
    
    class Customer {
        +bookEvent(Event)
        +cancelBooking()
        +addReview(Event)
        +viewMyTickets()
    }
    
    User <|-- Admin
    User <|-- Organizer
    User <|-- Customer
    
    class Event {
        +int id
        +String title
        +String description
        +Date date
        +Time time
        +String location
        +Float price
        +int capacity
        +String status
        +getEventDetails()
    }
    
    class Category {
        +int id
        +String category_name
        +getCategory()
    }
    
    class Booking {
        +int id
        +Float amount
        +String payment_status
        +String ticket_id
        +processPayment()
        +generateTicket()
    }
    
    class EventReview {
        +int id
        +int rating
        +String review
        +submitReview()
    }
    
    Category "1" -- "*" Event : categorizes
    User "1" -- "*" Booking : makes
    Event "1" -- "*" Booking : has
    Organizer "1" -- "*" Event : organizes
    User "1" -- "*" EventReview : writes
    Event "1" -- "*" EventReview : receives
```

## 3. Sequence Diagram (Booking an Event Ticket)
This diagram illustrates the chronological flow of messages between system components when a Customer books a ticket for an event.

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    actor Customer
    participant Frontend UI
    participant Backend API
    participant Database

    Customer->>Frontend UI: Clicks "Book Ticket"
    activate Frontend UI
    Frontend UI->>Frontend UI: Validate Inputs
    Frontend UI->>Backend API: POST /customer/create_order.php (user_id, event_id, amount)
    activate Backend API
    
    Backend API->>Database: Check event capacity (SELECT count)
    activate Database
    Database-->>Backend API: Return current bookings count
    deactivate Database
    
    alt Event is Full
        Backend API-->>Frontend UI: Error: Event Sold Out
        Frontend UI-->>Customer: Display Error Message
    else Event has Capacity
        Backend API->>Backend API: Process mock payment / generate ticket_id
        Backend API->>Database: INSERT INTO bookings
        activate Database
        Database-->>Backend API: Success (booking_id)
        deactivate Database
        
        Backend API-->>Frontend UI: 200 OK (Booking Successful)
        Frontend UI-->>Customer: Show "Booking Confirmed" & Redirect to Tickets
    end
    deactivate Backend API
    deactivate Frontend UI
```

## 4. Activity Diagram (Creating an Event)
Provides a visual representation of the workflow when an Organizer creates a new Event in the system.

```mermaid
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Login
    Login --> OrganizerDashboard : Valid Organizer Credentials
    OrganizerDashboard --> ClickCreateEvent : Selects Create Event Menu
    
    state CreateEventForm {
        ClickCreateEvent --> FillDetails : Fill Title, Date, Time, Venue, Price, Capacity
        FillDetails --> UploadCoverImage : Choose Image
        UploadCoverImage --> SubmitForm : Click 'Publish'
    }
    
    SubmitForm --> ValidateFrontend : System validates inputs
    
    ValidateFrontend --> FillDetails : [Validation Failed]
    ValidateFrontend --> BackendAPI : [Validation Passed]
    
    state BackendAPI {
        ProcessData --> SaveImage : Uploads Image to /uploads
        SaveImage --> InsertDB : INSERT INTO events
        InsertDB --> SuccessResponse : Returns JSON Success
    }
    
    BackendAPI --> ShowSuccessMessage : Frontend receives response
    ShowSuccessMessage --> OrganizerDashboard : Redirects back to Dashboard
    OrganizerDashboard --> [*] : End Flow
```
